//
// Source: Shaopu Han, Yanfeng Jiang, "Advanced hybrid MRAM based novel GPU cache system for graphic processing with high efficiency," AIP Advances, 14(1):015058, 2024
// DOI:    10.1063/9.0000721
// Tech:   SOT-MRAM
// Node:   16 nm
//
// Geometry (verbatim from the paper):
//   Verbatim, Sec. II: 'In contrast with STT-MRAM, the read and the write of
//   SOT-MRAM requires the synthesis of two transistors to consider separate
//   word and bit lines. Its peripheral circuitry will occupy a larger area.
//   This gap becomes more and more obvious with the increasing of the
//   storage capacity, much more than the 5% cell difference as shown in
//   Table I.' -> 2T1M with separate read/write word and bit lines. Also
//   'SOT-MRAM has separate read and write paths, which can effectively
//   reduce the mutual influence of storage and access operations and
//   increase the lifetime.' Cell area 57 F^2 vs STT 54 F^2 = 5.6% larger. At
//   F = 16 nm, 57 F^2 = 57 x 256 nm^2 = 14592 nm^2 = 0.0146 um^2. No MTJ
//   diameter, heavy-metal dimensions or layer thicknesses are given.
//
// Provenance: 15 reported, 2 derived, 2 assumed.
// WARNING - these values are NOT from the paper:
//   ReadMode = voltage  (Table I gives only Read Power. 'voltage' is the DESTINY default; NOT STATED by the paper.)
//   Temperature (K) = 300  (Not stated; assumed 300 K (mandatory key).)
// CHECK: key not in DESTINY grammar, will be ignored: 'TMR (%)'
// CHECK: assumed (not measured) values: ReadMode, Temperature (K)
// NOTE: PHYSICALLY SUSPECT CELL AREA vs TRANSISTOR COUNT. The paper says
// the SOT cell needs TWO transistors while the STT cell needs one, yet
// lists only a 5.6% area penalty (57 vs 54 F^2) and a LARGER access width
// (8.5 F vs 8 F). Taking AspectRatio at face value (57 F^2 at AR 0.57 ->
// ~10 F x 5.7 F), two transistors of 8.5 F width cannot be laid out side
// by side in a 10 F pitch. The paper half-admits this in Sec. II ('much
// more than the 5% cell difference as shown in Table I'), attributing the
// real gap to peripheral circuitry - but the .cell file itself still
// carries only 5.6%. THIS IS THE SINGLE MOST LIKELY SOURCE OF AN
// OPTIMISTIC SOT ARRAY MODEL.
// NOTE: SUB-100 ps PULSE BESIDE MULTI-ns SYSTEM TIMES. Set/Reset pulse of
// 0.1 ns is quoted alongside a 16 Mb external cache and 1500-2000 MHz core
// clock (0.5-0.67 ns period). A 100 ps write pulse is at the very edge of
// reported SOT precessional switching and leaves no margin for bitline
// settling; DESTINY will happily produce a sub-ns write latency from it
// that no real array achieves.
// NOTE: R_on = 165 kOhm is 55x the STT R_on (3 kOhm) in the same table,
// with no explanation. A 165 kOhm parallel-state MTJ at 16 nm implies an
// enormous RA product and will make read latency RC-limited; it is
// inconsistent with the very low 9.26 uW read power (9.26 uW into 165 kOhm
// implies V = sqrt(P*R) = 1.24 V across the MTJ, above any 16 nm rail).
// THESE THREE NUMBERS (R_on, R_off, ReadPower) ARE NOT MUTUALLY
// CONSISTENT.
// NOTE: No temperature, TMR, read current/voltage/pulse, min sense
// voltage, set/reset energy, or access-device drop/leakage.
// NOTE: Cell aspect ratio again equals CellArea/100 and is not independent
// information.
// NOTE: ReadCurrent solved by --auto-read; the paper's value did not admit
// a valid sense scheme at a safe MTJ read bias.

-MemCellType: MRAM                             // [reported] Table I column header 'SOT-MRAM'
-MemCellLevel: SLC                             // [reported] Single resistance pair, single set/reset pair in Table I.
-ProcessNode: 16                               // [reported] Table II, 'Process' = 16 nm
-Temperature (K): 300                          // [assumed] Not stated; assumed 300 K (mandatory key).
-CellArea (F^2): 57                            // [reported] Table I, 'Cell Area (F2)', column 'SOT-MRAM' = 57. NOTE: reported as 57, not 57.5.
-CellAspectRatio: 0.57                         // [reported] Table I, 'Cell Aspect Ratio' = 0.57 (again exactly CellArea/100).
-ResistanceOn (ohm): 165000                    // [reported] Table I, 'Resistance On (ohm)' = 165000
-ResistanceOff (ohm): 324000                   // [reported] Table I, 'Resistance Off (ohm)' = 324000
-ReadMode: voltage                             // [assumed] Table I gives only Read Power. 'voltage' is the DESTINY default; NOT STATED by the paper.
-ReadCurrent (uA): 1.2121                      // [derived] solved: 0.20 V bias ceiling / R_on 165000 ohm = 1.212 uA, giving 192.7 mV sense margin aga
-ResetMode: current                            // [reported] Table I specifies Reset Current -> current mode.
-ResetCurrent (uA): 54.02                      // [reported] Table I, 'Reset Current (uA)' = 54.02. Reset = AP->P. IDENTICAL to Set Current -> switchin
-ResetPulse (ns): 0.1                          // [reported] Table I, 'Reset Pulse (ns)' = 0.1 (= 100 ps)
-SetMode: current                              // [reported] Table I specifies Set Current -> current mode.
-SetCurrent (uA): 54.02                        // [reported] Table I, 'Set Current (uA)' = 54.02. Set = P->AP. Symmetric with Reset.
-SetPulse (ns): 0.1                            // [reported] Table I, 'Set Pulse (ns)' = 0.1 (= 100 ps)
-AccessType: CMOS                              // [reported] Table I row 'Access CMOS Width (F)'
-AccessCMOSWidth (F): 8.5                      // [reported] Table I, 'Access CMOS Width (F)' = 8.5. NOTE: the paper states the cell has TWO transistor
